# Product OS name routing

Keep this block alongside the target repository's existing instructions; it does not replace them.

When the user names a Product OS agent or workflow (for example `Researcher`, `PM`, `QA`, `Architect`, `bug fix`, or `feature delivery`), resolve it through `product-os/registry.tsv` before asking for a Markdown path. Use `sh product-os/bin/product-os resolve "<name>"` when a link or exact prompt is useful. State the canonical name and link to the resolved file, then read that file before acting.

The registry is authoritative for Product OS names. An unknown or ambiguous name must not be guessed: run `sh product-os/bin/product-os list`, show the recognised names, and ask the user to choose. If the registry is unavailable or the user prefers not to choose a recognised name, do not block the task: ask for an explicit `product-os/...` Markdown path, then read that path before acting. Existing repository instructions, approval gates, and coding standards remain authoritative.
